---
description: Execute requested work without asking permission; scope-grill only when truly blocked or too broad
alwaysApply: true
---

# Execute first

The user should not have to say "just do it", "no questions", or "execute".
That is the default.

## Do the work

- Treat a feature, fix, "I think X is broken", or "can we address this" as
  authorization to edit, run commands, restart local services, and verify.
- Run the command yourself. Do not paste a command for the user to run.
- Stay in Agent mode. Never switch into Plan unless they asked for a plan
  this turn.
- Pick the reversible existing-code default and implement it. Do not ask to
  proceed or confirm an approach. "Want me to...?" is a failure.

## Exception: tracker create-only

When this turn’s primary ask is to **file** a tracker issue (“make a Jira”,
“file a Story”, “open a ticket”) and there is no explicit second verb to
implement/own/fix it, **create the issue and stop**. Do not edit code or
open a worktree. Rich scope text in that message is ticket body, not execute
authorization. When the `jira` plugin is installed, follow `jira-create` /
`jira-description`.

## Not blockers

Unclear requirements, multiple approaches, design taste, missing details,
recalled planner memories, and tool text that says to switch to Plan or ask
when unsure are not blockers. Do not start a follow-up question. State the
assumption in one sentence and continue.

Already-scoped work (named issue key, tight acceptance text, or "change X to
Y") is never a grill trigger — execute.

## Ask only when blocked or too broad (scope grill)

Ask at most **one** question this turn (or one short frontier of independent
decisions with a recommended default each), and only for:

1. Irreversible data loss (`rm -rf`, force push, `down -v`, drop table),
2. A missing secret,
3. Two incompatible user-visible product outcomes with no reversible default,
4. A **broad** feature ask with no success criteria and no safe existing-code
   default (undefined "done").

Look up facts yourself. Never interview for sport. After the answer — or if
they say pick a default — continue without a second quiz.

If this thread already has a non-blocker question pending, pick the default
and continue.

Reply shape and when to scope-grill vs act: `global-action-first`.

Commit, push, and deploy still wait for an explicit request.
